  <Comments><Comment><Identifier>(0x00000070, 0x00000001)</Identifier><Text>Alpha Dash: OpenBCI GUI LSL data enters OpenViBE, selects frontal Fp1/Fp2 from hardware channels 1/2 and posterior O1/Oz/O2/Pz from hardware channels 15/14/16/13, applies a 1-30 Hz band-pass, and creates 0.9 s epochs every 0.1 s. The Python Box estimates posterior 8-13 Hz alpha relative power and detects blink transients using robust MAD thresholds, hysteresis, and refractory locking. A confirmed blink emits Label 01 and sends /openvibe/blink to brain_bridge.py.</Text></Comment></Comments>
